# Review: IndexCore

The convergence-key intent mechanism is solid: `IndexEngine` records intents inside the transaction
that writes the index rows, `ConvergenceKeyIntentStore` gives the record / take / clear contract with
an id-bounded clear (tested), and `EchoHost._runIndexPass` services the intents through
`ConvergenceKeyMerger` after the Automerge leg, clearing only serviced keys (exercised end to end by
the echo-client-e2e convergence tests). Everything new in this spec is missing: there is no
`IndexerIntent` union, no feed-options intent kind, store or table, no `setFeedOptions` on either
host, no indexing-disabled state in either `FeedDataSource`, and no removal of index rows when a
store trims blocks. The biggest gap against today's behaviour is F-4.1: EDGE's `FeedSpace` trims
feeds with `FeedStore.deleteOldestBlocks` and leaves their index rows behind.

## Extensions

| Term      | URI                        |
| --------- | -------------------------- |
| `verdict` | `org.dxos.mdl.verdict@1.0` |

